{"name":"Revival","hex":"#5f81a4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"revival","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of reviving, or the state of being revived.","Reanimation from a state of languor or depression; applied to health, a person's spirits, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/revival"}],"entries":[{"title":"Revival (comics)","blocks":[{"text":"Revival is an American horror comics series created by writer Tim Seeley and artist Mike Norton. The pair worked with colorist Mark Englert and cover artist Jenny Frison to produce the series, which was published by Image Comics as 47 monthly issues released between July 2012 and February 2017. It has since been reprinted in both paperback and hardcover editions that contain multiple issues."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c8/RevivalComic1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revival_(comics)","wikidata":"Q25204969"},{"title":"Revival (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Revival is a horror novel by American writer Stephen King, published on November 11, 2014, by Scribner. It tells the story of a former minister who becomes obsessed with electricity, and a man who knew him as a child."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/Revival_novel_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revival_(novel)","wikidata":"Q17028760"},{"title":"Revival (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Revival is a supernatural horror noir television series based on the American comic book series of the same name by Tim Seeley and Mike Norton, and published by Image Comics. Created by Aaron B. Koontz and Luke Boyce, the series premiered on June 12, 2025, on Syfy in the United States and CTV Sci-Fi Channel in Canada."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/Revival_%28TV_series%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revival_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q130542547"},{"title":"Revival (Selena Gomez album)","blocks":[{"text":"Revival is the second solo studio album by American singer Selena Gomez. It was released on October 9, 2015, by Interscope Records, her first album released through that label. Preparation for the album began in 2014, when Gomez left her previous label Hollywood Records. The record was influenced by a range of artists, particularly Christina Aguilera and her album Stripped (2002). Gomez co-wrote twelve of its sixteen tracks. The album reflects her journey since 2013, including the media scrutiny surrounding her personal life. As executive producers, Gomez, Danny D and Tim Blacksmith collaborated with Hit-Boy, Rock Mafia, and Stargate to achieve Gomez's new desired sound. Revival is primarily a dance-pop and electropop record, connected by a tropical beach sound, with lyrical themes revolving around love and confidence."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/42/Selena_Gomez_-_Revival_%28Official_Deluxe_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revival_(Selena_Gomez_album)","wikidata":"Q20719689"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/Creep_meets_Em.png/330px-Creep_meets_Em.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/Creep_meets_Em.png/330px-Creep_meets_Em.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Em is attacked by one of the creeps known as \"glowing men\". Art by Mike Norton and Mark Englert.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACreep_meets_Em.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/10.11.13TimSeeleyByLuigiNovi.jpg/500px-10.11.13TimSeeley